  "title": "Unified Title",
  "summary": "SBCO (Self-supervised Block Coordinate Optimizer) improves planning agents by leveraging self-supervised learning, while addressing the limitations of self-referential self-improvement methods. This work provides a new approach for self-modifying agents with a fixed meta-agent and avoids requiring explicit self-modification.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "SBCO uses approximate block coordinate ascent to decompose verifiers and harness policy for improved performance.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "SBCO matches or exceeds a customized self-modifying baseline while using 4-5.5 times less compute budget.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The framework introduces a Two-Gate guardrail to preserve statistical guarantees and ensure the boundary between learnable and unlearnable tasks.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
